From e40b04c6c0dab475327c98e75e4579a60d4e3fad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marios Andreopoulos <opensource@andmarios.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:01:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] goodixtls: reliable transport, session reuse and a
 rotation-tolerant matcher

Transport and protocol:
- Gate every SPI read on the sensor's interrupt line instead of polling
  the bus; reads that land while the MCU parses our frames stall the TLS
  handshake. The driver now refuses to run without the IRQ line.
- Keep at least 1 ms of idle bus before every write: the sensor silently
  drops frames sent back to back, which made handshakes fail at random.
- Force-unlock the MCU's TLS state (0xD5) before each handshake, and send
  TLS-OK (0xD4) after it.
- Keep framing intact when a frame is larger than the caller's buffer, and
  check the transport header checksum.
- Keep the TLS session across opens, checking the MCU state to see whether
  it is still live: fprintd opens the device for every authentication, and
  the sensor stopped responding after a few hundred sessions since power-on.
- Drop the session when an image record is lost or fails its MAC, so the
  next capture starts a fresh one.
- Request the IRQ line with edge detection and pull-up: after an S3 resume
  the firmware leaves that pad with its input buffer disabled.
- Resolve the GPIO lines once per open; open and captures run in worker
  threads; finger polling uses the SSM's delayed transitions.

Matching:
- Rigid (rotation up to 20 degrees + translation) geometric check with
  one-to-one candidate pairs and clusters of at least four points,
  decision threshold 12. On 58 labelled captures: naturally shifted presses
  accepted 11/20 (was 6/20), normal presses 10/10, other fingers all at 0
  (was up to 6).
- Report a verification as soon as it is scored, not once the finger is
  lifted.
- Integer descriptor distances (identical results, several times faster).

Also: OpenSSL's TLS1-PRF KDF for key derivation, one BIO method per
process, debug knobs and dead code removed, fixes from review (FDT
calibration from a finger-down background, image and memory-read length
checks, adaptive-store sweep using fprintd's hex finger names).

Protocol facts behind these changes come from public research:
lexakimov/goodix51c0_spi-reversing, delitdesnoyers06-del/goodix-gxfp-
protocol, szlukabence/goodix-fingerprint-spi-linux and goodix-fp-linux-dev/
goodix-fp-dump. No code was taken from them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
